source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"2027 NFL draft order projections for Round 1, chances for top pick, more","description":"ESPN's Football Power Index projects the 2027 NFL draft order for Round 1, complete with each team's chances to pick in the top five, in the top 10 and at No. 1.","published":"2026-11-27T11:00:02.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/draft2027/story/_/id/49794361/2027-nfl-draft-order-projections-first-round-picks","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN staff","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Can the 49ers lock up the NFC West after exceeding preseason expectations?","description":"The 49ers are 9-1, and two of their next three games are against the Seahawks (6-4) and Rams (7-4) at home.","published":"2026-11-27T11:00:13.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50582755/san-francisco-49ers-nfc-west-playoffs-seeding","type":"Story","byline":"Nick Wagoner","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"2026 NFL playoff picture: AFC, NFC seed projections, chances to make postseason","description":"We're looking ahead to how the 14-team playoff picture could line up -- and who will win divisions -- en route to the Super Bowl.","published":"2026-11-27T11:00:08.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/49745176/2026-nfl-playoff-predictions-afc-nfc-odds-super-bowl","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN staff","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Rashee Rice, Chiefs believe he caught pivotal 3rd-down pass late vs. Bills","description":"WR Rashee Rice -- along with several members of the Chiefs -- felt he caught the ball on a pivotal third-down pass with less than two minutes left at the Bills.","published":"2026-11-27T08:17:16.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50609968/rashee-rice-chiefs-believe-caught-pivotal-3rd-pass","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Nate Taylor","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Bills QB Josh Allen struggles vs. Chiefs in 'grossest' conditions","description":"The Bills won their 10th game of the season Thursday vs. the Chiefs, but QB Josh Allen struggled in the weather, passing for only 81 yards.","published":"2026-11-27T07:57:30.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50609813/bills-qb-josh-allen-struggles-vs-chiefs-grossest-conditions","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Nick Suss","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Eagles QB Joe Milton wows teammates with breakout game in Dallas","description":"Eagles QB Joe Milton had a breakout game on the national stage, accounting for four touchdowns in a wild 39-38 come-from-behind win over the Cowboys.","published":"2026-11-27T06:10:08.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50609081/eagles-qb-joe-milton-wows-teammates-breakout-game-dallas","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Tim McManus","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Bills edge Chiefs with last-second FG in low-scoring battle","description":"The Bills won their seventh straight, snapping the Chiefs' win streak at three in a sloppy, low-scoring thriller.","published":"2026-11-27T05:59:59.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50582828/2026-nfl-buffalo-bills-kansas-city-chiefs-thanksgiving","type":"Story","byline":"Nick Suss and Nate Taylor","source":"ESPN"}],"wiki":{"title":"Tyler Lacy","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tyler_Lacy","description":"American football player (born 1999)","touched":"2026-11-26T23:15:21Z","intro":"Tyler Lacy (born November 10, 1999) is an American professional football defensive tackle for the Detroit Lions of the National Football League (NFL). He played college football for the Oklahoma State Cowboys. Lacy was selected by the Jacksonville Jaguars in the fourth round of the 2023 NFL draft.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Lacy was born on November 10, 1999, in Garland, Texas. He is a cousin of former National Football League (NFL) player Aaron Ross, a Super Bowl champion with the New York Giants. He attended Sachse High School, being a consensus three-star recruit, and committed to play college football at Oklahoma State after his graduation from the school."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"As freshman in 2018, Lacy redshirted and saw no game action at Oklahoma State. The following year, he started all 10 games in which he appeared, missing three due to injury, totaling 20 tackles, including two for a loss, with one sack and two pass breakups. In 2020, he remained a starter and was named honorable mention all-conference after leading the team's defensive line with 32 tackles and eight TFLs, additionally posting four sacks and five quarterback hurries.\nLacy earned a second honorable mention all-conference selection in 2021, additionally being named to their first-team All-Academic squad as he posted 34 tackles, 11 for-loss, and 3.5 sacks. He also recorded eight hurries, the fifth-best in school history since they started tracking the statistic in 1982. His senior season in 2022 was cut short due to injury, and he finished it with 17 tackles, five quarterback hits and three sacks. Lacy finished his stint at Oklahoma State with 113 tackles, 30 for-loss and 11.5 sacks while appearing in 44 total games."},{"key":"career","title":"Professional career","text":"JACKSONVILLE JAGUARS\nLacy was selected by the Jacksonville Jaguars in the fourth round (130th overall) of the 2023 NFL draft. He appeared in 15 games and posted 12 tackles and a pass deflection in his first season.\nOn August 26, 2025, Lacy was waived by the Jaguars as part of final roster cuts.\n\nDETROIT LIONS\nOn August 27, 2025, Lacy was claimed off waivers by the Detroit Lions."}],"wikidataId":"Q117716061","family":[{"relation":"Relative","name":"Aaron Ross","description":"American football player (born 1982)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aaron_Ross"}],"social":{"x":"tylerlacy85","instagram":"tylerlacy85"}},"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4361861","pfr":"https://www.pro-football-reference.com/players/L/LacyTy00.htm","pff":"https://www.pff.com/nfl/players/tyler-lacy/76836","otc":"https://overthecap.com/player/tyler-lacy/10954","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tyler_Lacy"},"insights":["On the field for 32% of Detroit’s defensive snaps this season.","2026 cap number of $1.1M is the 36th-largest on the roster.","Contract expires after this season.","Drafted 130th overall in 2023 (round 4) by JAX."]}